#
# mob (hex package — a fork or a PR, NOT an app-owned edit):
#   Mob.Share.file/2 — deps/mob/ios/mob_nif.m + deps/mob/lib/mob/share.ex.
#     Mob.Share is text-only and `mix mob.enable file_sharing` has no Elixir
#     surface, so no Mob app can hand a file to the user. Kati's Android answer
#     is K-20 file-transport; iOS has none and is served by
#     UIFileSharingEnabled + LSSupportsOpeningDocumentsInPlace instead.
#   A notify NIF — :mob_nif has no notify entry at all in 0.7.20, so the
#     generated MobBridge.notify_schedule/notify_cancel are unreachable from
#     Elixir in every Mob app. See K-22 notify-and-periodic-bridge for the
#     shape Kati needed (a String reply, and an application context).
#   A C-linkage accessor for the cached bridge jclass — mob_ui_cache_class
#     already caches it (mob_nif.zig:1712) but keeps it in a Zig-internal, so
#     every project-owned NIF has to cache its own copy. See K-21.
#
# mob_new (templates — app-owned, so these are template fixes):
#   handleFilesResult should read OpenableColumns.DISPLAY_NAME rather than
#     uri.lastPathSegment, and build its JSON with org.json. See
#     K-20 file-picker-display-name; affects every Mob app that filters picked
#     files by extension.
